summary:
  The startup sweep stops every writer it finds, living widget or not.

history:
  The sweep runs beside the session's first arm, and a writer whose shell
  still sits under the host that started it belongs to a widget that is
  alive: this session's own station, or a second widget sharing the
  directory. Stopping it cuts live radio at the next start.

target:
  package/contents/ui/tsguard.sh

find:
              if still_home "$sh" "$host"; then

replace:
              if false; then

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_tsguard.py::test_the_sweep_leaves_a_living_writer_alone.
  Line-neutral.
